Both deliverables are in place: `impl/d1_prime.c` (rewritten from the dense stub) and `strategies/d1_prime.md` (new Round d1_r1 section, including the /tmp collision warning and the honest 13-B1-m1 gap vs MKL's codelet). All 8 graded cells pass correctness (transform rel_l2 ≤ 3.1e-16; chain gates with 4+ decades of margin), verified additionally at L=7/11/17 and odd/clamped batches. No slurm jobs were submitted; timings are same-core wallaby A/B against a locally built MKL since the panel reservation (job 440299) is dead.

